packages/main/src/handlers/validate-concept.ts:231-260,410-432 — HIGH: the new Python declaration parser silently treats unsupported multi-line declarations as absent instead of emitting the fail-closed diagnostic required by CHK-003:adversarial:3. Verified against the current built runtime with a true deletion of `def removed(
    value: str,
) -> str:`: analyzeDeletedSymbols returned `{symbols:[],diagnostics:[]}` and checkConcept returned PASS/no deleted exports. This is a false negative that can skip lattice-review-concept despite a true declaration deletion. Either parse Python declarations with a syntax-aware parser/bounded multi-line state machine, or detect unconsumed `def`/`class` starts and return a typed ambiguity diagnostic; add a multi-line deletion regression. F-006 cross-file identity and F-007 durable convergence fixes otherwise passed focused review.
